# Configuring the GitHub Report

The `github-changes` report reads the issues of the repository named in `<issueManagement>/<url>`, which must look
like `https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/issues/`. See the [goal documentation](../github-changes-mojo.html) for all
parameters.

Using GitHub Enterprise
-----------------------

No additional configuration is needed. The address of your **GitHub** instance is taken from
`<issueManagement>/<url>` in your POM.

Authenticating to the GitHub REST API
-------------------------------------

Anonymous requests to the GitHub REST API have a low rate limit. If you are using GitHub Enterprise or you want to
authenticate to GitHub, configure the server in `settings.xml` like so:

```xml
<settings>
  ...
  <servers>
    <server>
      <id>github</id>
      <password>YOUR-TOKEN</password>
    </server>
  </servers>
  ...
</settings>
```

Only the `password` item is used, as the token in `Authorization: Bearer YOUR-TOKEN`. It can be
[encrypted](https://maven.apache.org/guides/mini/guide-encryption.html).

The default serverId is `github`. You can change it by setting the `<githubAPIServerId>` configuration parameter.

See [Authenticating to the REST API](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/authentication/authenticating-to-the-rest-api)
in the GitHub documentation.

Filtering Issues
----------------

By default the report includes open and closed issues, but only issues that have a milestone.

#[[### Only include closed issues]]#

If you only want to include closed issues in your report, set `<includeOpenIssues>` to `false`. It is `true` by default.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-changes-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <includeOpenIssues>false</includeOpenIssues>
        </configuration>
        ...
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

#[[### Include issues without milestones]]#

If you also want to include issues that do not have a milestone attached to them, set `<onlyMilestoneIssues>` to
`false`. It is `true` by default.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-changes-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <onlyMilestoneIssues>false</onlyMilestoneIssues>
        </configuration>
        ...
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

#[[### Using the current version]]#

If you only ever want the current release in your GitHub Report, you can use the `<onlyCurrentVersion>` configuration parameter. It will take the version from your project's POM and try to match it against the milestone title of the GitHub issues.

Once you have configured this, you can forget about it, as it updates itself when you change the version number in your POM.

**Note:** The names of your milestones in GitHub must match the ones you use in your POM. The _-SNAPSHOT_ part of the version in your POM is handled automatically by the plugin, so you don't need to include _-SNAPSHOT_ in the names of your milestones in GitHub.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-changes-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <onlyCurrentVersion>true</onlyCurrentVersion>
        </configuration>
        ...
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

Selecting columns
-----------------

You can select which columns to include in the report. Valid columns for GitHub are `Assignee`, `Created`,
`Fix Version`, `Id`, `Reporter`, `Status`, `Summary`, `Type` and `Updated`.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-changes-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <columnNames>Type,Id,Summary,Assignee,Status,Fix Version</columnNames>
        </configuration>
        ...
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```
